# data/stats.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the committed snapshot the
# build falls back to when the GitHub API is rate-limited, which is common on
# shared CI IPs. See scripts/fetch-stats.ts.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only documents
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are working notes and tooling instructions, not part of the published
# project. They stay on disk and out of the repository.

# The original design brief. A long internal working document that describes an
# earlier design direction, kept locally for reference.
PORTFOLIO-BRIEF.md

# Raw source material for the /velra page. These hold real terminal captures:
# session ids, a local account name, private session titles and private prompt
# text. The site never reads them. It builds from data/velra/captured.json,
# which scripts/velra-transcripts.ts generates from the first file with every
# private value replaced by a visible placeholder. Keep both out of the
# repository; the second one embeds a full copy of the first.
VELRA-ALL-PROVIDED-TERMINAL-OUTPUTS.md
VELRA-CLAUDE-MASTER-PROMPT*.md

# Coding-agent instructions. AGENTS.md is regenerated by `next dev` on every
# run, so ignoring it is also what keeps `git status` clean.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
